        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Two valves together fill a tank in \\(4\\,\\mathrm{h}\\). The first valve alone takes \\(6\\,\\mathrm{h}\\) less than the second valve. Find the time taken by the first valve alone.",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Let the first valve take \\(x\\,\\mathrm{h}\\), so the second takes \\((x+6)\\,\\mathrm{h}\\). Then \\(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x+6}=\\frac{1}{4}\\), which gives \\(x^2-2x-24=0\\). Since \\(x>0\\), \\(x=6\\,\\mathrm{h}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 82,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
