        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A rectangular plot has perimeter \\(40\\,\\mathrm{m}\\). If one side is \\(x\\,\\mathrm{m}\\), the other side is \\((20-x)\\,\\mathrm{m}\\). If its area is at least \\(96\\,\\mathrm{m^2}\\), which interval contains all possible values of \\(x\\)?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The area condition is \\(x(20-x)\\ge 96\\), or \\(x^2-20x+96\\le 0\\). Since \\(x^2-20x+96=(x-8)(x-12)\\), the solution is \\(8\\le x\\le 12\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 84,
        "question_data": {
